+# Daily Grind components
+
+Load `components/index.js` once with a `<script type="module">`. The components use native custom elements and open Shadow DOM; no runtime framework or build step is required. Each module can also be imported separately.
+
+## Coffee card and hero
+
+`coffee-card` and `coffee-hero` accept three named slots: `heading`, `description`, and `action`. Keep headings at the appropriate level for the surrounding page, and use real anchors for navigation. Give repeated action links a descriptive accessible name.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="heading">Maple Oat Latte</h3>
+  <p slot="description">Oat milk with Vermont maple syrup.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/seasonal"
+     aria-label="View details for Maple Oat Latte">View Details</a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+Consumer content stays in the document and updates naturally through slots, without rebuilding the shadow tree or losing focus. Without JavaScript the text and links remain available.
+
+## Navigation
+
+`grind-navigation` takes branding in the `brand` slot and native anchors in the default slot. Add `data-logout` to an anchor for its outlined appearance. Each instance owns its menu state. At widths up to 640px, a native button toggles the links; Tab follows normal document order, and Escape closes the menu and restores button focus. Desktop links are always available. Resize handling moves focus when its previous target becomes hidden. Global viewport listeners are removed on disconnect and restored on reconnect.
+
+The disclosure button and its `aria-controls` target live in the same shadow root. The component uses ordinary navigation semantics rather than application menu roles.
+
+## Styling
+
+Component styles live in their shadow roots. Typography and the existing `--primary`, `--accent`, and other page tokens inherit normally. Components have standalone fallbacks for the tokens they consume. Override `--card-background` or `--hero-image` (a CSS `url(...)`) for local variants. Public parts are `card`, `hero`, `navigation`, and `toggle`.
+
+Slotted nodes belong to the consumer; page styles can deliberately override their default presentation. Keep page resets scoped so they do not unintentionally override slotted content. The host `hidden` attribute remains supported.
+
+## Checks
+
+Run `pnpm install` followed by `pnpm test` for automated DOM tests. These cover slots, separate shadow roots, disclosure state, same-tree ARIA references, focus restoration, viewport changes, reconnection, native link activation, and content without upgrades. They do not verify visual layout or substitute for assistive technology testing.
